WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:05.140
I guess it was a kind of different experience for us and for me.

2
00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:09.960
We were the first black graduates, first black law students.

3
00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:14.200
Except that the year before we entered in 1951,

4
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:25.220
Roy Wilson had been there as a student for a short time under the United States Supreme Court-ordered desegregation of the law school.

5
00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:33.340
Well, I know that in addition to your many distinctions you have the distinction of being the first black graduate of law school.

6
00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:40.140
What was it like being a pioneer, in a manner of speaking, at LSU law school?

7
00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:46.700
Well, I think that generally there was not a great deal of hostility to . . . in my opinion.

8
00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:54.220
There were some who shunned myself and [Robert] Collins, I guess.

9
00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.060
Some were cordial.

10
00:00:56.060 --> 00:01:03.100
They would speak to you when they were alone, but when they were with a group they might not say anything to you,

11
00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:08.320
because I guess they were fearful of being criticized by some of their white peers.

12
00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:15.080
And of course, we couldn’t use . . . You know, we couldn’t go in the facilities in Tiger Town.

13
00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:17.940
They were just off limits.

14
00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:21.200
The blacks couldn’t go in there.

15
00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:30.000
How did you feel that the faculty . . . law faculty regarded the change of events?

16
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.500
Well, I think the faculty accepted.

17
00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:37.060
I think [Dean Henry] McMahon was . . . I remember registration.

18
00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:44.140
I think he was very cordial, you know, friendly and told us that we were going to be treated like any other law student.

19
00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:46.444
I think that was the way it was by the faculty.

20
00:01:46.444 --> 00:01:55.333
I didn’t sense any overt or evidences of discrimination on the part of the faculty.

21
00:01:55.333 --> 00:01:59.620
If it was present, they didn’t manifest it.
